import-linter
# scripts/verify_discussion_report.py only -- the app must never import this.
# A blank report PDF is invisible to every in-app check (Mitra returns 200 with
# a valid, empty file), so verifying it means extracting the text.
pypdf

# Object storage for voice recordings, which go browser -> bucket via a
# presigned URL. boto3 covers AWS S3 and, through CLOUD_ENDPOINT, every
# S3-compatible service (OCI Object Storage, MinIO) -- see
# app/integrations/storage/aws.py.
boto3
# google-cloud-storage is deliberately NOT pinned here. It is needed ONLY for
# CLOUD_STORAGE_PROVIDER=gcp (or its gcs/gcloud/google aliases) and is imported
# lazily inside that branch, so an AWS or local deployment should not pay to
# install it. Install it explicitly when running against GCS:
#
#   uv pip install google-cloud-storage
#
# app/integrations/storage/gcp.py turns the resulting ImportError into a
# StorageConfigError naming that command. Verified against a live bucket with
# 3.13.1; the driver uses only Client/Blob/signed-URL APIs, which have been
# stable across 2.x and 3.x.

# gunicorn is deliberately NOT here. MITRA_ENABLED=1 requires a single worker
# process (MitraSessionManager pools live WebSockets in process memory), so the
# only thing a process manager would add is a way to violate that. Run uvicorn
# directly and scale with THREADPOOL_SIZE. See app/core/runtime.py.
